# Auth Rules

## Better Auth Structure
- Auth config: `src/lib/auth.ts` (server)
- Auth client: `src/lib/auth-client.ts` (client)
- API route: `src/app/api/auth/[...all]/route.ts`

## Reading Sessions
```ts
// Inside a Server Component
import { auth } from "@/lib/auth"
import { headers } from "next/headers"
const session = await auth.api.getSession({ headers: await headers() })

// Inside a Client Component
import { authClient } from "@/lib/auth-client"
const { data: session } = authClient.useSession()
```

## Route Protection
- Define protected paths via `src/middleware.ts`
- In Server Components, `redirect("/login")` if no session
- Perform role checks on the server side; use client side only for UI

## Blocking Unauthorized Actions
- Check session + role at the start of every Server Action
- If not authorized, use `redirect` or `notFound()` — do not `throw new Error("Unauthorized")`
